 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505351,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>If possible, subtract the following irrational numbers without using a calculator. If this is not possible, state why.</p>\n<span data-math=\"41\\sqrt {15}  - 23\\sqrt {15}\">41\\sqrt {15}  - 23\\sqrt {15}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"18\\sqrt {15}\">18\\sqrt {15}</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"41\\sqrt {15}  - 23\\sqrt {15} \"></span></p>\n<p>Because they have the same irrational part, you can subtract without using a calculator.</p>\n<p>The formula uses the distributive property: <span data-math=\"\\left( {a \\times x} \\right) \\pm \\left( {b \\times x} \\right) = \\left( {a \\pm b} \\right) \\times x\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {41 - 23} \\right) \\times \\sqrt {15} \"></span> Subtract.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"18\\sqrt {15} \"></span></p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
